00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,440
 In the context of the manufacturing techniques that we're talking about this week,

2
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:06,800
 welding and braising are processes for joining metals.

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:11,440
 While both welding and braising involve melting some kind of film metal to attach to

4
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:15,760
 other metals together, the key difference between these is that welding also involves

5
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:19,440
 melting the base metal, the parent metals, while braising does not.

6
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:23,200
 In this video we're going to talk about both welding and braising. The differences between these

7
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:27,520
 are when you might choose to use one technique over the other. We'll kick off by talking about

8
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:30,880
 welding, and you should note that there are many, many different processes that you can

